  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Kordofan Emergency WASH response to Displaced people in El Abbasiya and Abu Jubaiha IDP camps.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to provide 15,998 South displaced people are provided with safe, adequate sanitation and hygiene promotion services in El Abbasiya and Abu Jubaiha IDP camps and settlements in South Kordofan state.

Building on earlier responses by aid organisations to the health needs of the camps, CAFOD with its national partner SIDO will work to address the sanitation and hygiene promotion needs of 8,654 IDP in Alabasya and 7,344 IDP in Abu Jubaiha. Emergency latrines will be constructed; this will be accompanied by vector control campaigns, general cleaning campaigns, capacity strengthening, and hygiene promotion activities to raise awareness of good hygiene behaviour and the appropriate use of water and sanitation facilities, with WASH committees established to ensure the engagement of the communities.</narrative>
  </description>
